1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,280
The nearest VPS city is a reasonable
starting point, but it

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:06,860
is not proof of the best connection for
your users.

3
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,360
Network routes and the application itself
also matter.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,140
First, identify where the people using the
service connect

5
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:17,620
from. Do not choose a region only because
it is close

6
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,240
to the person paying the invoice.

7
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:24,500
Next, find the provider's documented test
facility or looking glass

8
00:00:24,500 --> 00:00:26,760
for the region, if one is available.

9
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:30,280
Follow its permitted use and compare from a
connection representative

10
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:34,280
of your audience. A result from one network
is an observation,

11
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,820
not a worldwide latency guarantee.

12
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:40,820
Record the region, test time, method and
result.

13
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:44,620
If you have not run a test, label the
choice as untested.

14
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:48,660
A polished map must not become evidence of
a measurement that never

15
00:00:48,660 --> 00:00:51,640
happened. Then consider the service.

16
00:00:52,160 --> 00:00:56,260
Static content behind a suitable delivery
layer behaves differently from an

17
00:00:56,260 --> 00:01:00,500
application that makes repeated requests to
a distant database.

18
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:03,720
Look at where the dependencies live as well
as the VPS.

19
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:08,740
Our take: make a small shortlist and a test
plan before making

20
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:13,140
a long commitment. A slightly different
route or dependency can matter

21
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:15,717
more than the city name on a plan card.

22
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:20,480
The location guide at vpsdealswire.com has
the full checklist.

23
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:25,300
Open the description link, compare your
actual requirements, and verify

24
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:27,280
the candidate region with the provider.

25
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,440
This video does not claim a lowest-latency
winner.
